id: hu-physical-training
name: Physical Training
system: heroes-unlimited
source_book: Revised Heroes Unlimited p.124-126
category: rcc
hit_points_base: "P.E. + 1D6 per level"
sdc_base: "30"
starting_money: "4d6x100"
bonuses: { pools: { hp: "2d6", sdc: "3d4x10" }, combat: { attacks: 1 }, saves: { coma_death_pct: 10 } }
skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { choose: 8, categories: ["Physical"], bonus: 20 }
    - { choose: 3, categories: ["Espionage"], bonus: 20 }
    - { choose: 1, from: ["Hand to Hand: Expert", "Hand to Hand: Martial Arts", "Hand to Hand: Assassin"], note: "Only an evil alignment may select Assassin." }
special_abilities:
  - name: "Power Punch"
    description: "3D6 damage. A super powerful punch drawing on one''s inner will, or chi. Counts as TWO melee attacks or actions."
  - name: "Power Kick"
    description: "4D6 damage. Like the power punch, it draws on the character''s inner reserves of strength to deliver a devastating blow. Counts as TWO melee attacks or actions."
  - name: "Force of Will"
    description: "The ability to stay on one''s feet after S.D.C. and hit points have both fallen to zero or below. In that state the character has only ONE attack per melee, no power punch or kick is possible, speed is halved, and every bonus to strike, parry and dodge falls to zero - natural, unmodified dice only. He can function for 24 hours or until hit points reach -40, whichever comes first, and then collapses into a coma. Minus 40 is below his P.E. limit and he would usually be beyond saving; force of will and physical condition keep him alive, but only professional treatment brings him back, to 2 hit points, recovering at the usual rate. Blood loss still applies below zero: 1 hit point per minute, stoppable with first aid or paramedic skills."
restrictions: ["Do NOT select any physical skill as a scholastic or a secondary skill choice - the eight physical skills above take their place", "The educational level grants ONE SKILL PROGRAM FEWER than it prints"]
extraction_notes: "THE BOOK CONTRADICTS ITSELF ABOUT WHETHER THIS CHARACTER ROLLS FOR EDUCATION. Printed 27 says outright that the Physical Training and Special Training categories ''do NOT roll on the Educational Level Table''; printed 124, this category''s own STEP TWO, says ''Roll to determine the character''s educational level as usual. Then subtract one skill program selection.'' The category''s own step is followed, because it is the specific rule and it states a modification that only makes sense if the roll happens. The two deductions it carries - one program fewer, and no physical skills chosen scholastically - are in `restrictions`, where a reader meets them; neither is enforceable, because a program count lives on the OCCUPATION and this is the race half of the pair. THE NINJAS AND SUPERSPIES OPTION is not stored: printed 124 allows any one of 38 martial arts from that book in exchange for five physical skills, three espionage skills and half the secondary skills. It is another book''s catalog, and this repo imports what it has read. THE THREE SPECIAL ABILITIES ARE NOT A CHOICE - every physical training character has all three - so they are named definitions with no choice group over them. Power Punch and Power Kick carry no `bonuses`: `combat.punch` and `combat.power_punch` are strike bonuses on the sheet, not damage dice, and the damage is what the book states."
---

## Lore

Not all heroes are instilled with an extraordinary super ability or possess a
super-science gizmo. Some rely entirely on their own natural abilities. They are
the super athletes, who have honed their physical bodies into finely tuned
fighting machines of flesh and blood which have reached the pinnacle of physical
perfection. Heroes who rely on their strength, agility, skills, cunning and
courage.

The physical training character''s power is his own superior physical body. He is
tougher, faster and stronger than most professional athletes, and alongside
building and mastering that body he has trained in the arts of combat.

Although any weapon, gimmick or vehicle can be used, this character is most
comfortable with hand to hand and ancient weapons. He has moulded his body into
a living weapon, and to reach for an accessory such as a sub-machinegun is to
ignore the power of that living weapon. Far better the elegant and silent bow:
it obeys the body and mind without resistance and becomes an extension of
oneself, while the automatic weapon shrieks and coughs and jumps with a life of
its own. That is generally this character''s philosophy about arms and combat -
almost always preferring the silent, obscure and more natural forms - and it is
usually wise, because he is most deadly in all forms of hand to hand combat.

## GM Notes

**Write the physical attributes down in pencil.** Almost every physical skill
selected adjusts one of them, and hit points and S.D.C. are determined LAST for
the same reason. All bonuses are cumulative, and careful selection of physical
skills is most of what designing this character consists of.

A hand to hand combat skill is one of the areas of physical expertise rather
than an extra, so it is chosen above. The character gets the usual two attacks
per melee plus one as a bonus; anything further comes from boxing and combat
experience.

**The Ninjas and Superspies option**, printed 124: with the G.M.''s approval the
player may take any one of the 38 martial arts hand to hand skills and abilities
from that game instead, forfeiting FIVE physical skills, THREE espionage skills
and HALF of his secondary skills. In the terms of that book the character is a
"Worldly" Martial Artist. Those 38 skills are not in this catalog.

Unless the character is extremely wealthy, only conventional weaponry and body
armour are available. Any alignment may be chosen, though heroes should
generally be of good alignment - and only an evil one may take Hand to Hand:
Assassin.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-physical-training');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-physical-training';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-hu-physical-training-class.sql');
